+Lobe Reordering is a step to reorder the SGGX lobes within each voxel so that lobes with the same index across different voxels have similar shapes, enabling shared weight factors [S2]. This is critical when using voxel clustering where weight factors are shared among multiple voxels [S2]. The process involves: 1. Picking an arbitrary voxel $i$ as a reference and keeping its lobe ordering fixed [S2]. 2. For each other voxel $i'$, finding a permutation $\pi^*_{i'}$ of $\{1..m\}$ that minimizes the L2 difference between corresponding SGGX normal distributions $D$ [S2]. 3. Applying $\pi^*_{i'}$ to reorder the lobes of voxel $i'$ [S2]. The optimal permutation is found by minimizing:
 $$ \pi^*_{i'} = \arg \min_{\pi} \sum_{j=1}^{m} \int (D_{i,j}(m) - D_{i',\pi(j)}(m))^2 dm $$
 Since the number of lobes $m$ is usually very small, $\pi^*$ can be computed via brute-force search [S2].
